&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">kn...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;&gt;  What does &quot;this_is_a_stupid_string&quot; do?<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; I don&#39;t know. In the runr package this is a random string instead. I have<br>&gt; not tried to understand what is its role (I was too busy with understanding<br>&gt; the rest).<br>&gt;<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Le mercredi 8 avril 2015 20:29:44 UTC+2, Yihui Xie a écrit :<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Interesting. Thanks for sharing! What does &quot;this_is_a_stupid_string&quot; do?<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; As I said, pull requests are welcome:<br>&gt;&gt; <a href="https://github.com/yihui/runr/issues/11" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/yihui/runr/issues/11&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355038526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2VQ85FW9g93A44s1bLU_RP">https://github.com/yihui/runr/issues/11</a><br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Regards,<br>&gt;&gt; Yihui<br>&gt;&gt; --<br>&gt;&gt; Yihui Xie &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">xiey...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Web: <a href="http://yihui.name" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yihui.name&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355038526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2C_N319Oj3J3n9F_i8M3KI">http://yihui.name</a><br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; On Wed, Apr 8, 2015 at 12:46 PM, &#39;Stéphane Laurent&#39; via knitr<br>&gt;&gt; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel="nofollow">kn...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Hello, just for sharing : <a href="http://rpubs.com/stla/72006" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rpubs.com/stla/72006&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792355038526000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2KdQjdy2HqY5ktwOum_UC8">http://rpubs.com/stla/72006</a><br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Source Rmd :<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; library(knitr)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; split_results &lt;- function (x, sep) # function borrowed from runr package<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; {<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;     x = strsplit(paste(x, collapse = &quot;
&quot;), sep)[[1]]<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;     res = vector(&quot;list&quot;, length(x))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;     for (i in seq_along(x)) {<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;         el = gsub(&quot;^
+|
+$&quot;, &quot;&quot;, x[i])<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;         res[[i]] = if (i%%2 == 1)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;             structure(list(src = el), class = &quot;source&quot;)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;         else paste(el, collapse = &quot;
&quot;)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;     }<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;     res<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; }<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; knit_engines$set(V8 = function(options) {<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;   code &lt;- as.character(c(options$code))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;   output &lt;- ct$eval(code)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;   code &lt;- lapply(split_results(code, sep=&quot;this_is_a_stupid_string&quot;),<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; function(x) knitr:::wrap.source(x, options))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;   if(options$results==&quot;hide&quot;) return(code)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;   else return(c(code, knitr:::wrap.character(output, options)))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; })<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Load `V8` and define a new context named `ct`:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; library(V8)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ct &lt;- new_context()<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Define `x` in Javascript context using the chunk option `engine=&#39;V8&#39;`:<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r, engine=&#39;V8&#39;}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; var x=[];<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; x.push([1,2]);<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; x.push([3,4]);<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; x.push([5,6]);<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; JSON.stringify(x)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Get `x` in R :<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ( x.in.R &lt;- ct$get(&quot;x&quot;) )<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Double `x` in R and assign in Javascript context :<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ct$assign(&quot;double_x&quot;, 2*x.in.R)<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r, engine=&#39;V8&#39;}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; JSON.stringify(double_x);<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; Load a Javascript library :<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ct$source(system.file(&quot;js/underscore.js&quot;, package=&quot;V8&quot;))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```{r, engine=&#39;V8&#39;}<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; JSON.stringify(_.flatten(x))<br>&gt;&gt; &gt; ```<br>&gt;&gt; &gt;<br>&gt;<br>

